       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks wrong.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg is 5 times the maximum daily dose.** For adults, amlodipine is usually 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg is the maximum. A 50 mg dose would put the patient at risk of severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia and shock. Amlodipine overdose is hard to treat because the drug stays in the body for a long time (half-life of about 30\u201350 hours).\n\nThe most likely explanation is a typo for **5 mg**, which is a common starting dose for an adult with normal liver function.\n\nCan you confirm the dose you want? For example:\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg by mouth, once daily**, or\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg by mouth, once daily**, or\n- another dose within the usual range.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter it right away."
